1
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,960
The greatest harem

2
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,960
Lightly leaping over these hectic times

3
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:37,460
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,460
I wanna dive into paradise

5
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:42,160
Nothing but the latest trends

6
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,080
So you can wear them

7
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,220
Because a bare face is
what sells on the spot

8
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,880
Let it rain

9
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:55,000
Everybody can do, we started running

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

11
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,500
Let's set sail for tomorrow

12
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,280
Let it run

13
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:07,680
Everybody can do, just a little

14
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,820
Even if we step out of line, it doesn't hurt

15
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,000
Holding onto a noisy curiosity

16
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,000
We soared strong and high

17
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,840
Declaration of Chakote Number Four

18
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,540
It's even colder today, isn't it?

19
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:46,320
Nothing's going to happen
on a night like this anyway.

20
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:49,100
Let's skip the patrol and head home already.

21
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,340
Molester!

22
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,480
Isn't this the Katsushika police box?

23
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,520
You bold, fearless...

24
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,480
Nakagawa, you go around to the front.

25
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:57,860
Yes.

26
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:05,800
Where, where? Where's the molester?

27
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,820
Hey, those are your underwear!

28
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:10,320
Molester!

29
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:30,980
Panty thief, Ryotsu!

30
00:02:31,140 --> 00:02:34,660
If it's Kankichi Ryotsu, it wouldn't be
strange at all even if he were a panty thief!

31
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:37,920
Got him! Arrest! I'm arresting you!

32
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:40,280
Caught red-handed for underwear theft!

33
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,920
Don't be ridiculous!
I'm not some underwear thief!

34
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,300
Then what's that you're
holding in your hand?

35
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,460
That's the undeniable evidence!

36
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:57,280
N-no! I just grabbed this
in a panic when I fell!

37
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:00,180
I came in here because I heard a scream.

38
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:02,740
Do you really think that excuse will work?

39
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:03,980
It's true.

40
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,580
There's another one here?

41
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:06,400
That's not right, is it?

42
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:09,960
Nakagawa?

43
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:11,180
No way.

44
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:12,880
It's a misunderstanding.

45
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:16,180
We came in here after hearing a scream
that said there was a chikan.

46
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:16,920
It's no use.

47
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,280
I already said that.

48
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,240
So that's what happened.

49
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,440
Oh no, we said it and
caused a misunderstanding.

50
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,460
I'm sorry.

51
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:27,180
Now that you mention it, we were practicing
our anti-chikan squad drills.

52
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,860
Did we shout "chikan"?

53
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,420
Look, you two.

54
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,040
We're saying the exact same thing,

55
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,780
but you don't believe a
word I say from the start.

56
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,800
You don't even question
what Nakagawa says, do you?

57
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:39,180
Well, of course, that's only natural.

58
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,880
Obviously.

59
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:44,600
What grounds do you punks
have for judging people?

60
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,920
Well, obviously it's the face, right?

61
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:49,500
Anyway, a guy with eyebrows that
are joined together like that,

62
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,460
with that sweltering, oppressive face,

63
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:53,160
there's no way his words can be trusted,
is there?

64
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,120
That's right, and on top of that,
your legs are stubby.

65
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,080
Rustling around,

66
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,080
shameless,

67
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:59,300
short as you are, with a long torso,

68
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:00,780
and on top of that, your feet stink.

69
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,200
You lot, saying whatever you want!

70
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,340
Hey, please stop.

71
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:05,920
Senpai, let go!

72
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:07,780
That sound... could it be?

73
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,000
Stop it, idiot, stop it!

74
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,320
Ryo-san.

75
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:15,220
No, it was a misunderstanding!

76
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:18,980
Nakagawa-san says you tried to steal underwear,
didn't you?

77
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,060
I've told you, I didn't!

78
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,580
I'm innocent!

79
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,980
That's rough luck, Ryotsu.

80
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:38,640
But getting into a situation like that

81
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:40,820
is because of how you behave day to day.

82
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,740
You'd better reflect on that properly.

83
00:04:43,740 --> 00:04:45,760
Reflect? Don't be ridiculous.

84
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,500
Honestly, these days those women

85
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,460
what do they think men are?

86
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,560
I can't say I don't understand that.

87
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,960
Sure, these modern women,

88
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,380
they're beyond my understanding.

89
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:57,280
Just the other day, too...

90
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,220
What a bummer.

91
00:05:00,220 --> 00:05:00,940
Right?

92
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:02,360
So, you see,

93
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:04,120
she says it with this
pitiful look on her face.

94
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:05,640
"We're begging you, please go out with us."

95
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,400
But...

96
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:08,060
Ew, what's that supposed to be?

97
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,740
Hey, you don't even have any money!

98
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,040
Hey, old man.

99
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:13,300
What have you been
staring at this whole time?

100
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,920
N-no, I wasn't looking at anything!

101
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,600
Pervert.

102
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:18,620
Man, that really got to me.

103
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:20,600
Frankly, that one's an alien.

104
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,540
I've made up my mind!

105
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,580
What are you doing, senpai?

106
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:28,900
I've decided once and for all,
I won't deal with women anymore!

107
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,300
Within two meters of me,

108
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,120
I will never let a woman come near!

109
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:34,960
That's ridiculous!

110
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,200
But then you can't do your job!

111
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:38,220
Yeah!

112
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,460
Excuse me.

113
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,440
Which way is the station?

114
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,020
No, no!

115
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:48,180
D-don't you dare come within that line!

116
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:52,180
W-what did you say?
You're a police officer, aren't you?

117
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:54,383
The station, right?

118
00:05:54,433 --> 00:05:57,540
The station is the first corner,
to the left...

119
00:05:58,220 --> 00:06:00,860
You, you, you, idiot!

120
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,340
No matter what anyone says,
I'll never have anything to do with women.

121
00:06:12,220 --> 00:06:13,700
What a shame.

122
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:17,640
We almost had that Ryotsu arrested.

123
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,960
Really, really.

124
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:21,640
In front of Ryo...

125
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:29,620
Why is there a log in the
women's dormitory garden?

126
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:33,840
Naoko, something terrible's happened!

127
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,400
What is this log?

128
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:37,900
You're Naoko, right?

129
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:39,880
Congratulations on your election victory.

130
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,420
I see.

131
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,980
Remember, that's the one we won.

132
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:47,200
That magazine's giveaway.

133
00:06:47,820 --> 00:06:49,420
We entered on a whim,

134
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:51,700
and I never expected we'd actually win.

135
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,820
But Ryo's garden has plenty of room,
so it's fine, isn't it?

136
00:06:54,820 --> 00:06:55,680
Yeah.

137
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,000
Looking at Ryo's vest...

138
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,680
Lovely.

139
00:06:59,280 --> 00:07:01,500
Well, the delivery of
the materials is complete,

140
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:04,400
so this is the assembly
instruction video for the log house.

141
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:06,640
Now, please do your best to assemble it.

142
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:14,080
Are we going to build it?

143
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,480
What should we do? We can't assemble this.

144
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,760
Does anyone know someone who's
good at this kind of thing?

145
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:23,780
Found one!

146
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:28,240
But they'd never do it, would they?

147
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:32,940
I've got a good idea. Hey, hey.

148
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,900
Tomorrow, let's get everyone to pitch in.

149
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,820
Hey, hey, this is bad, Ryo-san.

150
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:42,280
Look at this month's survey
article in the internal newsletter.

151
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,600
Yeah, who cares about that.

152
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:47,180
Every single month they keep
running these boring projects.

153
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,400
Honestly, that's sexual harassment.

154
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:50,860
It's making fun of men.

155
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:53,880
Let's see, let's see... Ryotsu is the most hated again,
ranked number one?

156
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,060
So he's finally reached V7, then.

157
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,080
What's wrong?

158
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:04,340
W-What's this?

159
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:07,760
In the survey of Katsushika station's female officers,
for "most disliked"

160
00:08:08,820 --> 00:08:15,480
his name isn't listed. In fact, Ryotsu
is ranked number one for popularity.

161
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,840
Number one in favorability: Ryotsu Kankichi.

162
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,800
Number one as a lover: Ryotsu Kankichi.

163
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,620
Number one to marry: Ryotsu Kankichi.

164
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:31,340
Beating Nakagawa, who's always on top,
he's the triple crown winner!

165
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:35,460
Isn't this some kind of misprint?
That can't be right, can it?

166
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:37,580
Maybe if it were a typo or
a missing character, but...

167
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,040
So that means

168
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:42,360
You've been pulling some underhanded trick behind our backs again,
haven't you?

169
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,120
Why would I do something like that?

170
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:49,180
Senior, I don't think you'd go out of your way
to do something that doesn't make you any money.

171
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:51,460
Come to think of it, you're right.

172
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:54,280
But to go straight to first
place after reuniting like this...

173
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,900
That's strange, isn't it?

174
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:57,180
It's not strange at all.

175
00:08:57,740 --> 00:09:00,380
At last,
the women of today have finally realized it.

176
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:02,120
True manliness, that is.

177
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,420
They've started choosing
substance over appearance.

178
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:10,660
Ryo-senpai

179
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:12,900
Number one in likability!

180
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,480
Congratulations.

181
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:16,220
Congrats on coming in first.

182
00:09:16,700 --> 00:09:18,000
Ah

183
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:21,720
We've been misunderstanding you, Ryo-san.

184
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,340
That's right.

185
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:24,940
We've finally realized how charming you are,
Ryo-senpai.

186
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,340
I-I'm popular!

187
00:09:27,340 --> 00:09:28,720
I can't believe it.

188
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:32,100
Aw, you're making me blush.

189
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,160
Weren't you saying you
wouldn't deal with women?

190
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:38,020
What an unsociable guy.

191
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:41,300
Alright, don't you dare cross that line.

192
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:45,600
I've decided I'm not
dealing with women anymore.

193
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,620
Don't say that.

194
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,280
Shut up and get out!

195
00:09:49,280 --> 00:09:51,300
Shut up!

196
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:52,780
Senpai.

197
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:53,040
Says who?

198
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:54,920
Get lost, you hear me?

199
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:57,720
W-what's with that attitude?

200
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,740
Now, now, calm down.

201
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:02,400
Phase one is complete, for now.

202
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:05,860
That idiot's bound to take the bait,
after all.

203
00:10:11,680 --> 00:10:18,940
How's this? Like this?

204
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,940
Yeah, not bad, right?

205
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:22,540
He's here!

206
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,680
He's here! It's Rairai-ken.

207
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:29,520
Yes! Does he think that
disguise is fooling anyone?

208
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:33,760
Ramen delivery! One ramen, coming through!

209
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:41,780
I knew it. Ryotsu-senpai's appeal is his manliness,
isn't it?

210
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:46,640
Yeah, he has a sturdiness you just
don't find in the other men around here.

211
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:49,840
And those connected
eyebrows look so dashing.

212
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:53,540
Really, a good man is about
substance over appearance.

213
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,120
But it's sad, isn't it.

214
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:59,080
That he won't accept our
passionate feelings like this.

215
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:01,458
You know how we are, right?

216
00:11:01,508 --> 00:11:04,080
We always end up pushing
back against the men we like.

217
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,000
It's just that kind of personality...

218
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,040
Ryo-sama!

219
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:09,800
But he's pretty popular, isn't he? That guy.

220
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:15,240
So you tend to push back
against the man you like

221
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:19,640
Well, a woman's heart is pretty complicated,
I suppose.

222
00:11:21,280 --> 00:11:23,520
Well, well, well, hello there, you two!

223
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,160
Senpai Ryotsu!

224
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:26,592
Senpai,

225
00:11:26,642 --> 00:11:30,180
you wouldn't accept our bouquet earlier...

226
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:32,860
Naoko was really sad, you know.

227
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,260
Well, I'm sorry about that.

228
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:40,000
A canned coffee?
Nice, on a cold day like this.

229
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,520
Just give me a sip.

230
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,280
What, you're opening the can yourself...

231
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:43,940
Naoko

232
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,000
Please, go ahead.

233
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,780
Really?

234
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,360
Really?

235
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,620
Mm, that's good. Here, you drink some too.

236
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:53,780
Eeh!

237
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:57,660
Don't hold back, drink up.

238
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:59,300
B-but...

239
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:03,126
I'm so happy,

240
00:12:03,176 --> 00:12:05,060
Ryo-senpai

241
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:12,980
Yahoo!

242
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,200
Whoa!

243
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:15,780
Ho-ho-ho!

244
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,140
Hehehehe!

245
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:18,420
Yahoo!

246
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,380
Ho-ho-ho-ho!

247
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,380
Eek!

248
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,000
Why does this have to happen to me?

249
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,020
You held on well, Naoko.

250
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,160
Good, good.

251
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:34,180
We won't let your noble
sacrifice go to waste.

252
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:36,600
Now all that's left is
the finishing touches.

253
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:41,140
Hey!

254
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:53,860
Hey! Mr. Ryotsu!

255
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:58,900
Good evening, are you free?

256
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,960
What do you say?
Want to go out for drinks like old times?

257
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,360
Aaaaah!

258
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,900
I thought who it was. It's Honda!
Good to see you're doing well.

259
00:13:11,900 --> 00:13:13,940
W-what's going on? What's with that outfit?

260
00:13:14,420 --> 00:13:17,700
I've got an appointment tonight, you see.

261
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:21,060
Sorry, but I don't have
time to hang out with you.

262
00:13:23,100 --> 00:13:26,620
Apparently Ryo-san's been invited
to the women's dormitory tonight.

263
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:28,880
To the women's dormitory? The senpai?

264
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:33,780
I know you're jealous,
but I can't take you along.

265
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:37,780
After all, only I,
the most likable officer, was invited.

266
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:44,000
Honestly, these days women really know what's good about a real man,
don't they?

267
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,640
That's totally different
from what you usually say.

268
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:54,120
Good evening, ladies of the dormitory!

269
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:09,680
You know this place is strictly
off-limits to men, right?

270
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:12,520
Only Senpai Ryotsu gets
this special treatment.

271
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:16,260
Well, I'm touched.

272
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:19,420
Well, this is a predicament.

273
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:22,700
Naoko

274
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:24,897
Ryotsu-senpai,

275
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:28,480
The moon is so beautiful tonight.

276
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:29,560
Let's go and see it.

277
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:32,340
It was cloudy when we came here earlier.

278
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:33,820
Come on, come on.

279
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:37,260
Okay, now!

280
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:38,420
Roger that.

281
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:48,500
Isn't this the legendary master Bichūnen?

282
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:49,460
*Squeeze*

283
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:55,560
What's that?

284
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:58,420
That? It's a log house kit.

285
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:04,200
All the log materials are here, so you just assemble them following the blueprints,
and the gas and water connect with one touch.

286
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:07,840
If we build it in Ryo's yard, it'd
become a place where everyone can relax.

287
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,880
But the most important part,
the log builder, is missing.

288
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,840
We can't assemble it, though.

289
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:17,460
Isn't there some strong,
rugged man around here somewhere?

290
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:18,740
Nope, there isn't.

291
00:15:18,740 --> 00:15:21,640
Men these days are all so soft, aren't they?

292
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:25,340
A man who works up a sweat
is so charming, though.

293
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:26,200
Right, right.

294
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:29,700
The latest trend is men who smell of sweat,
isn't it?

295
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:31,820
Trend or whatever, I don't know about that.

296
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:34,520
Hey, haven't you two forgotten someone?

297
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:35,980
Forgotten who?

298
00:15:36,380 --> 00:15:39,700
A man who's strong, rugged,
and reliable, of course.

299
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,920
Who's that?

300
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:48,020
You don't mean Senior Ryotsu, do you?

301
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:51,500
No way, we can't ask Ryotsu-senpai for that.

302
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,800
Why not?

303
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:53,312
Because,

304
00:15:53,362 --> 00:15:57,720
Ryotsu-senpai went to all the trouble
of dressing up sharp in a suit like that.

305
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:58,220
Right?

306
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,720
This is just my temporary appearance.

307
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,700
This is my true form!

308
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:13,060
And this is my army!

309
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,640
Even though it's such a hit,

310
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:17,100
you're being so pushy.

311
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:19,060
Shut up, stop your nagging!

312
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:20,760
First, the foundation work.

313
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,320
You understand, you bastards?

314
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:26,700
Charge in!

315
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:30,100
Hey, get moving and work briskly!

316
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:32,500
Seriously, what's with that wimpy stance?

317
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,500
Men are so simple-minded.

318
00:16:41,000 --> 00:17:01,820
!

319
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:04,040
Thank you, Terai and Honda.

320
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:05,680
Please do your best, okay?

321
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,180
You're so reliable.

322
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:10,940
Honda, you're much more
robust than you look.

323
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:11,640
Is that so?

324
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,720
Terai, you also look like
you have powerful arms.

325
00:17:14,720 --> 00:17:17,520
No, I'm almost going all out.

326
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:19,400
You two, just go home already.

327
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,420
Damn, I messed up.

328
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:24,540
But you came all this way...

329
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:26,600
It'd be better if everyone pitched in.

330
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,960
I can handle this on my own, no problem.

331
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,140
Come on, go home, go home.

332
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:31,180
Not yet, not yet.

333
00:17:38,700 --> 00:17:40,500
That was a bit of a tactical blunder,
wasn't it?

334
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:50,040
Maybe doing it alone
was impossible after all.

335
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:52,540
We can't ask those guys for help now.

336
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:54,800
As expected, the pace is slow.

337
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,060
If that's the case,
we'll praise him thoroughly

338
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,140
and flatter him non-stop to get him working.

339
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,160
Okay.

340
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:04,880
Alright, hang in there and do your best!

341
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:09,120
Your working figure is so wonderful!
So cool!

342
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,040
R-really?

343
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,700
Wow, I'm so surprised!

344
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:15,540
What incredible strength!

345
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:16,960
What's this? I love it!

346
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:19,360
Wonderful!

347
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,780
You're so manly!

348
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:22,200
I see.

349
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,240
Those arms are the best!

350
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,980
Parker is easy to handle, isn't he?

351
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:31,500
Let's keep him hooked like this,
taking turns around the clock.

352
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:35,080
Yay!

353
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:37,600
Wow!

354
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,140
What a sucker!

355
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,620
Alright!

356
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:47,340
Alright!

357
00:18:47,340 --> 00:18:52,460
Alright!

358
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,040
See you!

359
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,960
Looks like 1,000 yen alone isn't enough

360
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,960
We need to give him a bit of
a shot in the arm about now.

361
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,580
Ryo-san, are you all right?

362
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,200
I'm a little tired.

363
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:12,760
I'll give you a massage. Hang in there!

364
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,800
Hurry up and build our log house, okay?

365
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:18,100
Of course, Tomoe!

366
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:19,900
Revived!

367
00:19:20,420 --> 00:19:21,520
Yay!

368
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:22,720
Alright, let's do this!

369
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:28,360
Good luck!

370
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:38,940
Here's your lunch.

371
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,020
See you.

372
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,720
You're already leaving?

373
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:42,940
It's for work.

374
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:45,680
Convenience store bento again?

375
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:49,040
It used to be a lovingly handmade bento.

376
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,980
As the house gets more complete,

377
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:51,600
the quality of the bento goes
down in inverse proportion.

378
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:53,940
The bento's grade keeps dropping.

379
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:58,420
This again?

380
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:01,040
Days of plain bread rolls and butter

381
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:01,720
are going to continue

382
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:04,880
Nobody's even come to cheer us on lately,

383
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,540
it's like we're being forced
into labor or something.

384
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,860
If we keep this up,
we're going to wreck our bodies.

385
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:13,820
I don't know, Senpai, but it feels like

386
00:20:13,820 --> 00:20:16,620
those women have you neatly
wrapped around their fingers.

387
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:18,240
Nakagawa-kun.

388
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:20,820
Having lost the top spot to me,

389
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,240
I understand your heartfelt longing.

390
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:23,580
Envy me all you like.

391
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:25,480
Don't go reading too much into it.

392
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,600
I don't really think it's
something to envy, though.

393
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:38,520
Man, I'm really tired now.

394
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,320
Senpai, Senpai Ryotsu.

395
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:46,200
Ryotsu-senpai, senpai.

396
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:49,700
Looks like that Ryotsu hasn't shown up yet.

397
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:50,660
He ditched us.

398
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:53,100
We're almost there,
but he's no help at all, is he?

399
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:55,640
When will this finally be finished?

400
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:57,480
I'm sick of flattering him.

401
00:20:59,580 --> 00:21:03,100
After all that work to get
him ranked first in the poll.

402
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,540
Just a little more patience.

403
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:07,260
Sorry.

404
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:08,780
I didn't mean any harm.

405
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:13,600
What? Did you say something?

406
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,320
Nothing, nothing.

407
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,720
Don't mind it.

408
00:21:18,720 --> 00:21:21,580
Alright, one more push. Let's do our best!

409
00:21:21,580 --> 00:21:23,960
Good, looks like he didn't hear.

410
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:25,720
Good thing he's a complete idiot.

411
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,280
He can hear you.

412
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:36,600
He's watching.

413
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:46,240
Wow!

414
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:46,760
How lovely.

415
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:48,420
So it's finally finished.

416
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:50,120
Our holiday villa.

417
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:52,380
Wow!

418
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:52,940
Amazing!

419
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:53,760
Incredible!

420
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:56,820
Curtain windows.

421
00:21:58,080 --> 00:22:00,940
The bath is bigger than the blueprint!

422
00:22:01,460 --> 00:22:03,400
Hey, let's stay here tonight.

423
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:04,520
Agreed!

424
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:09,760
Do you know what happens
when you make me angry?

425
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:11,940
I'll make sure to teach you properly.

426
00:22:18,740 --> 00:22:20,980
I like this woodsy scent.

427
00:22:20,980 --> 00:22:23,800
It feels like we're at a hot
spring deep in the mountains.

428
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:27,460
But still, I never expected
they'd build such a fine log house.

429
00:22:27,460 --> 00:22:28,920
That guy's more capable than I thought,
isn't he?

430
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:32,800
Yeah, he really did work hard.

431
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:34,980
I've gone and changed my
opinion of him a little.

432
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:37,460
Komachi-chan

433
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:38,840
W-what is it?

434
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:40,780
You've fallen for Kankichi Ryotsu,
haven't you?

435
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,500
Don't be ridiculous!

436
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:44,960
That scared me.

437
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:46,100
No, that's not it.

438
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:48,683
Everyone,

439
00:22:48,733 --> 00:22:50,840
please be quiet.

440
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:52,980
Front-row seats are 5,000 yen.

441
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:56,300
Anyone bringing a camera or
video camera owes 1,000 yen.

442
00:22:56,900 --> 00:22:58,140
Alright, here we go.

443
00:22:59,300 --> 00:23:00,380
Heh heh heh.

444
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:02,520
Divine punishment! You idiot women!

445
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,380
Woooah!

446
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:07,720
What?

447
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:28,720
See that?
This is what real man's work looks like!

448
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,040
What have you done! You brute!

449
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:35,340
Terrible!
The mini-patrol car is totally wrecked!

450
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:37,980
This is the worst!

451
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:40,660
Unforgivable!

452
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:44,440
The revenge is far from over!

453
00:23:44,980 --> 00:23:47,560
Bullying a delicate woman
like this is unforgivable!

454
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,040
Where exactly are you delicate?!

455
00:23:50,580 --> 00:23:51,420
Wait, wait!

456
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:54,880
Looks like you'll be hated again
and back on top as number one.

457
00:24:05,080 --> 00:24:07,100
A New Year's party at the Chief's house?

458
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:08,900
I didn't hear anything about that!

459
00:24:08,900 --> 00:24:11,700
Why didn't anyone invite me?

460
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:15,300
Chief, I'm on my way right now, you hear?

461
00:24:15,300 --> 00:24:17,880
Make sure you save some osechi for me.

462
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:20,500
Next time: New Year's Battle Karuta!

463
00:24:21,420 --> 00:24:21,720
See you then.

464
00:24:51,420 --> 00:25:03,460
Even if it's raining today,
tomorrow the sun will shine.

465
00:25:04,280 --> 00:25:13,840
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye
to all the things we don't like.

466
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:21,500
Oh yeah, let's try living
the way we want.

467
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:24,000
Good things are coming.

468
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:30,300
The sun is calling you
from outside the door.

469
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

